# APDS-9999 Kernel Driver

## `tests/` README

This directory contains the test suite for the APDS-9999 kernel driver.

Be aware that this was created by generative AI and should be treated as such.
I did not review the generated code. It is intended to help with the physical testing, nothing else.

It is structured as follows:

- static/ : contains static test cases which try the possible configurations of the driver.
            It considers edge-cases and checks the working of the driver under various settings.

- dynamic/ : contains dynamic test cases which may need interaction with the driver.
             There are automated tests that ensure the measurements are actually happening
             and then there are interactive tests that require user input to the sensor.

- dynamic/kernel-tools: contains some utilities used by the dynamic tests.

To run the tests, cd into the respecive directory (static or dynamic) and run `sudo bash run_tests.sh`.
This will go through the different test files `text_0x_*` and run them sequentially.


## kernel-tools README

This directory contains two little utilities for testing events and buffers of the iio subsystem.

The source code was downloaded from the [Linux kernel repo](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/tree/master/tools/iio).

I modified the iio_generic_buffer.c, such that it returns the exit code 0 on success. (Line 762)

The makefile is a simple version that just compiles the two utilities. It is not from the source above.
